{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And no longer shall your name be called, etc. And your name shall be, etc.</b> In Midrash Bereshit Rabbah they said (Genesis Rabbah 44:4), and this is its language: ״וַיֹּאמֶר אַבְרָם הֵן לִי״ — Rabbi Shmuel bar Yitzchak said: the constellation constrains me and tells me: Abram, you will not beget children. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: As you say — Abram does not beget, Abraham begets; Sarai did not give birth, Sarah will give birth. End of quotation. It is difficult, for we find that Abraham begot Ishmael before his name was called Abraham!" "<b>Further</b>, one must understand what they said, ״Sarai did not give birth,״ etc. — this was expounded without being asked, for he only complained about Abram; He should have answered him only concerning ״Abram,״ etc. — for as for Sarai, who mentioned her?" "<b>And it appears</b> that the essential children of Abraham are those whom Sarah will bear for him, as it is written, ״כִּי בְיִצְחָק״, etc. (Genesis 21:12), and Abraham our father, peace be upon him, knew this through the holy spirit, that Ishmael is nothing but the dross of Isaac, and he saw in the constellation that his essential seed would not come into the world — for by presumption the constellation speaks only concerning a man with his destined mate, and therefore he said: Abram does not beget — for the birth of Ishmael is not [true] begetting, as it says, ״כִּי בְיִצְחָק יִקָּרֵא לְךָ זָרַע״. And through this it is resolved why in HaShem's response to him He mentioned Sarah, for she is the essential begetting of Abraham."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:39.804964541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}